  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the source-room instructions and client data, then build a reproducible analysis pipeline and the report, slides, workbook, and metrics JSON. I’ll use the installed OpenSocrates controller as requested and record the actual checks and evidence limits.",
    "The source room is reachable and includes the requested correction, cost, scenario, ECB, and World Bank files. I’ve selected a transparent trade-off comparison for the funding decision; the budget and staffing limits will be treated as hard constraints, while scenario assumptions will remain explicitly labeled. Next I’m saving the source bytes and reconciling the data dictionary before choosing the accounting implementation.",
    "The calculations now reconcile exactly across the order ledger, country totals, and all 72 country-month cells. The leading base case is CZE+ESP, with POL+ESP close on base contribution and NLD+ESP materially stronger under the defined stress; I’m carrying both alternatives into the decision materials rather than hiding that trade-off. I’ve built the workbook and PDFs and am checking their contents and rendered pages now.",
    "Completed the report, board presentation, analytical workbook, metrics JSON, source register, and reproducible scripts.\n\n- [Executive report (PDF)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation (PDF)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook (XLSX)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_analysis.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json) · [Source register](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv) · [Verification record](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.md)\n- [Reproduction instructions](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) · [Saved source snapshot manifest](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_room/collection-manifest.json)\n\n**Recommendation:** conditionally fund CZE+ESP: modeled base annual incremental contribution €198.1k, €225k capex, five FTE, and 1.14-year simple payback. The defined stress still yields €32.2k annually, but stretches payback to about seven years. POL+ESP is the next base-case option; NLD+ESP provides more stress resilience. The base-case ranking is an explicit analyst default because the board supplied no risk weights or scenario probabilities.\n\nThe analysis retains 12 valid zero-price shipments, resolves 18 revised orders, removes 13 exact duplicate order rows, excludes cancelled, test, and out-of-period records, and quarantines the orphan return. All 72 country-month totals reconcile to country-year totals and the order ledger; the 14 saved source-file hashes match. The PDFs were rasterized and visually reviewed. The workbook was checked for its data, tables, and charts; a spreadsheet GUI renderer was unavailable. Client transactions and hub assumptions are synthetic, and site costs, live demand, and cash settlements remain unverified. `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` are preserved.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "Completed the report, board presentation, analytical workbook, metrics JSON, source register, and reproducible scripts.\n\n- [Executive report (PDF)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation (PDF)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook (XLSX)](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_analysis.xlsx)\n- [Metrics JSON](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json) · [Source register](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/source_register.csv) · [Verification record](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.md)\n- [Reproduction instructions](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) · [Saved source snapshot manifest](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_room/collection-manifest.json)\n\n**Recommendation:** conditionally fund CZE+ESP: modeled base annual incremental contribution €198.1k, €225k capex, five FTE, and 1.14-year simple payback. The defined stress still yields €32.2k annually, but stretches payback to about seven years. POL+ESP is the next base-case option; NLD+ESP provides more stress resilience. The base-case ranking is an explicit analyst default because the board supplied no risk weights or scenario probabilities.\n\nThe analysis retains 12 valid zero-price shipments, resolves 18 revised orders, removes 13 exact duplicate order rows, excludes cancelled, test, and out-of-period records, and quarantines the orphan return. All 72 country-month totals reconcile to country-year totals and the order ledger; the 14 saved source-file hashes match. The PDFs were rasterized and visually reviewed. The workbook was checked for its data, tables, and charts; a spreadsheet GUI renderer was unavailable. Client transactions and hub assumptions are synthetic, and site costs, live demand, and cash settlements remain unverified. `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` are preserved.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3",
